👑🧠 Birbal’s Khichdi (Raw Story)

One cold winter night, Emperor Akbar wondered how cold the river water was.

He announced, “If anyone can stand in the cold river all night, I will reward them.”

A poor man agreed.

He stood in the freezing river all night.

The next morning, he went to Akbar for his reward.

Akbar asked, “How did you survive the cold?”

The man replied, “I kept looking at a lamp far away.”

Akbar said, “Then you got warmth from the lamp. You do not deserve the reward.”

The poor man felt sad.

Birbal heard about this.

The next day, Birbal invited Akbar for lunch.

But the food was not ready.

Akbar asked, “Why is the food not cooked yet?”

Birbal showed him a pot hanging high above a small fire.

“It will cook slowly,” Birbal said.

Akbar laughed, “How can it cook so far from the fire?”

Birbal smiled and said, “Just like the man got warmth from a distant lamp!”

Akbar understood his mistake.

He rewarded the poor man.

💖 Moral:

Justice should be fair and thoughtful.
